finite `‖·‖_μ`.

**(b) Amputated amplitudes, and the normalisation they are measured in.**
For a source `O`, `M_1^O(h)` is its amputated one-hard amplitude and
`M_2^O(k,h)` its connected hard-plus-soft amplitude in the physical channel;
